'## Coverage and key history','','The bank grew 20 → 66 → 77 → 78 → 79 → 80. It contains **20 seeds, 52 qualifying additions and eight retained overlapping regressions**. The overlaps (Q38, Q41, Q44, Q45, Q46, Q52, Q60, Q61) remain in every full test but do not count as new source coverage. No hard question was removed. The [coverage/rejection ledger](coverage-ledger.json) records accepted novelty, rejected candidates, source mappings, historical stopping failures and the two final clean zero-addition passes **24 and 25**. A fresh source/key reviewer independently upheld them with no further additions or corrections: [final coverage PASS](coverage-review-08.json), [current coverage status](coverage-status.json). This is saturation under the stated scope/novelty rule, not enumeration of every possible combination.','','Question IDs and wording are preserved. Four answer targets required source-backed completeness corrections, transparently versioned before the final test:','','- [v6 Q37](benchmark-v6/key-corrections.json): broad wood production includes Daylight Overwork, not just Birdsong.','- [v7 Q04](benchmark-v7/key-corrections.json): one ready undamaged Vagabond hammer per crafting icon.','- [v8 Q07/Q12](benchmark-v8/key-corrections.json): hidden ruin shuffle/return and ordinary Eyrie Recruit placement.','- [v9 Q07](benchmark-v9/key-corrections.json): initial shared-deck shuffle before dealing.','','Original entries and hashes remain intact within their own benchmark versions. Every other prior answer is unchanged. The [final readable bank]('+B.name+'/question-bank.md), [questions]('+B.name+'/questions.json), [key]('+B.name+'/answer-key.json) and [benchmark hashes]('+B.name+'/input-manifest.json) are preserved separately. Q25’s shorthand means treating birds as the prompted suit, not bird-first selection or extra quantity.','',
'## Summary repairs and independent audit','','Repairs corrected faction setup, crafting costs and destinations, battle timing/scoring, dominance/coalition conditions, Keep/hospitals, the wood network, Decree/turmoil/leaders, Alliance supporters/Outrage/Train/Organize, and Vagabond quests/items/relationships. General rules and procedure tables were clarified; no scenario answer key was appended to the summary. Per-iteration diffs retain the changes. An early independent audit rejected an unsupported Revolt placement prerequisite; it was removed.','',('The final stamped-text auditor is a new Sol/high source-only agent, distinct from earlier auditors and every repair/key/grading actor. It read the complete summary, authoritative text and all 32 PDF pages; it inspected symbol-bearing PDF renders. Actual delivered read-call outputs and exact ordered source-line coverage are preserved in the [source auditor delivery audit]('+I.name+'/source-auditor-delivery-audit.json). It received no questions, key, reader outputs, grades or prior audit history and authored no repairs.' if stamped else 'The final independent auditor was fresh at its full audit, authored no summary repairs, and never saw questions, key, reader responses or grades. It checked the full applicable source, then verified every subsequent exact-text update.')+' [Final exact-text source audit]('+I.name+'/source-audit.json), '+('[fresh stamped source-only audit](expanded-iteration-12/source-only-audit/source-audit.json)' if stamped else '[fresh full-source audit](source-audit-candidate-07/source-audit.json)')+', [final audited source snapshot]('+audited_snapshot+'). No material findings remain.','','The Law delegates printed faction-track values and individual card/quest faces to physical components; those exact values are not reconstructed or invented. The audit also does not verify inherited play-time catalog metadata. These recorded source limitations do not leave an essential procedural ruling gap in this scoped test.','',
'## Reader isolation and model provenance','','Each iteration used two new **gpt-6-luna / high** readers with `fork_turns="none"`; primary/source/question reviewers used **gpt-6.1-sol / high**. Actual settings and independent session identities are confirmed from runtime `session_meta` and `turn_context`, not directory names or requested labels: [runtime evidence](runtime-model-provenance.json), [final pair provenance]('+I.name+'/model-provenance.json). Isolation is fresh context plus explicit two-file access instructions, not a stronger filesystem jail.','','The quote/apply/check process began with the coordinator-authorized [v5 protocol](reader-protocol-v5-template.txt) in iteration10. Stamped iteration14 introduced the generic [v6 operational refinement](reader-protocol-v6-template.txt): consecutive groups of at most five and programmatic nonempty exact-quotation checks. [Change note](reader-protocol-v6-change-note.json). Iteration15 added the generic [v7 refinement](reader-protocol-v7-template.txt): complete relevant procedural passages, specific per-clause entries, and the same ten-question-per-turn schedule for both readers, each group at most five. [V7 change note](reader-protocol-v7-change-note.json). One original fresh reader session handles the full80, with only generic continuation prompts; saved installments are retained. No rule facts, expected clauses, key or grade feedback are supplied; older scores are not changed because of a new process. It distinguishes question-stated scenario givens from summary-only rules authority, requires bounded complete input reads, relevant source quotations, per-clause applications and a self-check. This generic process supplies no rules facts. Iteration 10 kept candidate16 summary bytes, questions and key unchanged from iteration 9; the protocol change did not regrade earlier attempts. Both readers received identical text except output path, saved before dispatch: [A prompt]('+I.name+'/reader-a-prompt.txt), [B prompt]('+I.name+'/reader-b-prompt.txt), [protocol provenance](reader-protocol-provenance.json), [dispatch metadata](agent-dispatch-manifest.json). No question/key answer facts were leaked. Runtime dispatch message bodies are encrypted; their hashes and clear model/fork/task metadata are retained, while the final prompt plaintext copies and visible tool inputs preserve the new protocol. Older raw reader outputs and visible tool-history prompts remain unchanged.','',
'Actual input delivery was checked against runtime read-call/output pairs for '+str(delivery_count)+' reader sessions: [delivery audit](reader-delivery-audit.json). Ordered exact matching blocks, raw outputs, hashes, requested caps, truncation markers and recovery ranges are retained; declared line-number prefixes alone are removed for comparison. This proves delivery rather than cognitive attention. Iteration 9 A had a [confirmed delivery gap](expanded-iteration-09/delivery-defect.json): the ordinary-removal VP table and following note were lost across the initial truncated output and recovery ranges. That failed run and its factual grades remain, flagged as affected; no score was changed because of delivery. The final pair separately proved complete delivery of the frozen summary and all questions. Iterations 6 and 7 retested identical candidate13 bytes under the same protocol; the repeated attempt is explicit in the iteration 7 manifest.','',
